## 2.1.x.x User Form

### a. UI Specifications

#### <<User Form Screen>>

**Brief Description**
This screen allows the **System Administrator** to create a new user account or update an existing user account. It provides input fields for user information and supports validation before saving data.

**Mockup Screen(s)**
[Insert mockup/screenshot of **User Form Screen** here]

**UI Description / UI Requirements / Notes**

| No. | Component / Field       | Type                | Description / Requirement                                                                                                                      |
| --- | ----------------------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1   | Screen Title            | Label               | Displayed as **User Form** at the top of the screen. In create mode, title may be **Create User**; in edit mode, title may be **Update User**. |
| 2   | Full Name               | Textbox             | Allows actor to enter full name of the user. Mandatory.                                                                                        |
| 3   | Username                | Textbox             | Allows actor to enter username for login. Mandatory in create mode. Read-only in edit mode if the system does not allow username change.       |
| 4   | Email                   | Textbox             | Allows actor to enter email address. Mandatory. Must follow valid email format.                                                                |
| 5   | Phone Number            | Textbox             | Allows actor to enter phone number. Mandatory. Must follow defined phone format.                                                               |
| 6   | Password                | Password field      | Allows actor to enter password for the new account. Mandatory in create mode. Hidden input.                                                    |
| 7   | Confirm Password        | Password field      | Allows actor to re-enter password for confirmation. Mandatory in create mode.                                                                  |
| 8   | Role                    | Dropdown            | Allows actor to assign one role to the user, such as Admin, Director, Sales Staff, Production Manager. Mandatory.                              |
| 9   | Status                  | Dropdown / Toggle   | Allows actor to set status as Active or Inactive. Default is Active when creating a new user.                                                  |
| 10  | Save Button             | Button              | Saves the entered data after validation.                                                                                                       |
| 11  | Cancel Button           | Button              | Cancels the operation and returns to previous screen.                                                                                          |
| 12  | Reset Button            | Button              | Clears editable fields on the form or restores original values in edit mode, depending on system design.                                       |
| 13  | Validation Message Area | Inline text / Label | Displays field validation messages when input is invalid.                                                                                      |

**UI Requirements / Notes**

* The same screen is used for both **create** and **update** actions.
* In **create mode**, password and confirm password are required.
* In **edit mode**, password fields may be hidden if password is changed in a separate screen.
* Mandatory fields must be clearly marked.
* The system shall validate all input before saving.
* If validation fails, the system shall display error message near the relevant field or at the top of the form.
* Clicking **Cancel** shall discard unsaved changes after confirmation if data has been modified.
* Only authorized users, normally **System Administrator**, can access this screen.

